      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story\nAsset type: production atlas of four independent widescreen backgrounds for a first-grade arithmetic lesson about a community kite festival supply station. The mathematical quantities will be added in code.\nComposition: landscape 16:9 atlas, exactly four equal 16:9 panels in a 2 by 2 grid, hard crop boundaries exactly halfway across and down, no outer border, no dividers, no bleed between panels. Each quadrant must work as an independent complete widescreen picture when cropped. Keep the central 70 percent of every panel quiet and unobstructed.\nTop left: outside a little park supply stall seen at child's eye level, quiet empty pale counter in the foreground, pine green canopy and a single distant apricot diamond kite tucked into a corner. Warm spring daylight.\nTop right: close, almost straight-on view of the empty workshop counter for a falling tile game; creamy paper-lit wall, muted spruce pegboard shapes only at the edges, no pegs in the middle, no tools or trays on the central counter.\nBottom left: directly overhead view of a flat empty pale apricot paved workyard for a top-down delivery game. Soft foliage at the far side corners only, no pavement seams in the middle, no roads, traffic, buildings, boxes or perspective.\nBottom right: another independent view of the same park stall in soft late afternoon, very subtle warm apricot light and quiet empty wooden work surface. Open edges and tidy silhouette.\nStyle: premium picture-book game art, fine matte gouache paper grain, crisp cut-paper silhouette, warm cream and deep pine green with muted apricot and persimmon accents. Gentle value separation, restrained detail, clean silhouettes.\nAvoid: any counted objects, people, packages, numbers, words, labels, symbols, watermark, UI, grids, borders, signage, or typography. No gradients or glassmorphism.",
